    "result_text": "There's only the one acceptance test class, and the full build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe E.164 telephone validation is centralized in `OwnerTelephone.toE164` (used by `RequireOwnerFields`, `ApplyOwner`, and `RequireUniqueTelephone`), so I added the per-country national-number length check there rather than in each pipeline step.\n\n`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerTelephone.java`:\n- After the existing generic 8\u201315 digit check, the national-number length is now validated against the country code: `+61` requires 9 national digits, `+1` requires 10. A wrong length throws `InvalidTelephoneException`, which the existing `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` maps to **400 Bad Request**.\n- Only the two country codes with a known fixed length are enforced; other codes (e.g. `+64`) keep the generic rule, so existing valid numbers are unaffected.\n- Updated the class javadoc to document the new rule.\n\nThe new test (`+61 123` \u2192 400) passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
